    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n**Before:** the agendas were rows nested in one narrow \"Agenda\" box and showed no content.\n\n**After:**\n- One box per agenda (`sp-dashboard-agendas`), in a grid of `sp-dashboard-agenda-columns` (fewer if the window is narrow), `sp-dashboard-agenda-box-width` wide, so they grow sideways and down.\n- Each lists its 3 most urgent open TODOs, wrapped to 2 lines and cut with an ellipsis. Urgency = priority + near/overdue deadline + scheduled today or earlier + `NEXT`/`PROG`. Deadlines lists the nearest deadlines. Files come from the existing `sp-dashboard-agenda-*-files`, or `org-agenda-files`.\n- **Privacy:** private entries (tag `private`, or files matching `sp-dashboard-private-files`) are never inserted while the dashboard is public. `P` cycles auto / public / private; in auto, `sp-dashboard-public-conditions` decides and a check that errors counts as public. The list is empty by default; Wi-Fi and screen-share checks are provided but inert until configured. `g` redraws.\n- Doc and CHANGELOG updated; the doc tangles to the `.el`.\n\n**Checked** (Emacs 29.3, headless, sample Org files): ranking, wrapping, grid, public hiding, error → public, `TAB` through the boxes. **Not checked:** a GUI, your real agenda files or speed on a large `org-agenda-files`, and the Wi-Fi / screen-share checks.\n\n**Choices:** TODO lines are not buttons by default (each would add a `TAB` stop); `sp-dashboard-agenda-todos-clickable` turns that on.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01T2BcMQ3qdNUiW5oZRLQRsG)_",
